{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_012NB1VTj3sGW1kQu62RTJio","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vz3eXkjj5X3EwZVUtX2QGR","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md","old_string":"- **AC-5.3**: End-to-end determinism: the whole sequence replayed on a fresh thread produces byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files.\n\n- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3): Replay on a fresh thread → hash equality on every pull output and the materialized file.","new_string":"- **AC-5.3**: End-to-end determinism: the whole sequence replayed on a fresh thread produces byte-identical pull outputs, and a materialized file that is byte-identical after normalizing only the intentionally random thread id (threads design decision 7) — the two runs' thread ids must differ and every other byte must be exact. Pull outputs carry no thread id, so their equality stays literal with no normalization. (See Spec Deviations: ruling-011.)\n\n- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3): Replay on a fresh thread → literal hash equality on every pull output; materialized-file hash equality after substituting only the random thread id, asserting the two thread ids differ and every other byte is exact."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6157,"cache_read_input_tokens":47374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6157},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be","uuid":"23d50c07-7024-487e-8bd2-765b31c9e2ba","request_id":"req_011CbycXiavKKLzN1xPY1KpB"}
