{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CJRoBSp1MmGPrA9vbeFdV9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Story 4 requirements source now records the ruling. Done — scope was the doc only; no production code or tests touched.\n\n## What I changed\n\nUpdated `docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md` to record the ruling captured in `artifacts/04-lifecycle-exercise/ruling-011-response.json` (decision: *accept threadId-normalized materialized-file equality and update story spec*). The story's AC/TC/DoD previously claimed flatly \"byte-identical … materialized files,\" which contradicted the ruling and the test header's pinned deviation.\n\n- **AC-5.3 / TC-5.2** (replay): materialized-file equality holds **after normalizing only the intentionally random thread id**, with the two thread ids asserted to differ and every other byte exact; **pull-output hash equality stays literal** (no normalization).\n- **AC-5.4 / TC-5.3** (teardown): same threadId-only normalization for the materialized file; final pull byte-identical and health deep-equal.\n- **Test Mapping** rows for TC-5.2/TC-5.3 reworded to match.\n- **Spec Deviations** changed from \"None.\" to a full record of ruling-011: context (threadId is threads design decision 7's one random value, embedded in the session header; a literal byte match would require a forbidden test-only id seam), the accepted contract for both legs, why pull equality stays literal, and an explicit \"not a weakening\" note.\n- **Definition of Done** line aligned.\n\n## Notes\n\n- I kept scope to the **story file** (\"the Story 4 requirements source\"), per the ruling's own `update-story-spec` decision. The same \"byte-identical pull outputs and materialized files\" phrasing is also restated in three other docs in this spec-pack — `epic.md:149,156,157`, `stories/coverage.md:48`, and `test-plan.md:38`. I left those untouched. Say the word if you want them aligned to the recorded ruling too.\n- One thing worth flagging: the recorded ruling says **both** replay and teardown \"assert the thread ids differ,\" but in `test/lifecycle.test.ts` only the **replay** leg (TC-5.2) has `expect(replay.threadId).not.toBe(run.threadId)` — the teardown leg (TC-5.3) relies on it differing by construction (fresh thread) without asserting it. I did not change the test (your guardrail was doc-only / no weakening). If you'd like the teardown leg to assert id-difference explicitly so the implementation matches the recorded contract exactly, that's a one-line *strengthening* addition I can make."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2665,"cache_read_input_tokens":58674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2665},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceae9c6b-d571-491c-ba4d-0d8e5cb3a7be","uuid":"f7c26b14-60fd-4724-a9a5-d4d0645aaf56","request_id":"req_011Cbycc767xHhnmDfdguEEG"}
